Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: lru-fs
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, fuse3
Description: scratch filesystem: recently used files in RAM, the rest on disk
 lru-fs is a FUSE filesystem for scratch space (AI agents, builds, test
 clones, temporary downloads). Files live as plain files in a RAM tier
 (tmpfs) and a disk tier: recently used ones stay in RAM up to a budget,
 the rest move to disk, files untouched for a few days are deleted, and a
 size cap or minimum free space trims the least recently used first.
 .
 Ships a systemd user unit that mounts ~/scratch:
   systemctl --user enable --now lru-fs
